# Copy to .env and fill in the CURRENT session's SSH port+password for the
# remote machines (Machine A is this local sandbox/orchestrator and isn't
# listed here). Kaggle (or whatever host you're on) mints new port/password
# pairs each session, so this file is meant to be re-filled every time, not
# committed.
#
# Only B/C available (no MTP)? cp this to .env, fill in B/C, ignore D, then
# run ./cluster/qwen35_122ba10b_3machine.sh. Full 4-machine/MTP cluster?
# Fill in B/C/D too - see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the manual bring-up.
MACHINE_B_PORT=9194
MACHINE_B_PASSWORD=changeme
MACHINE_C_PORT=9195
MACHINE_C_PASSWORD=changeme
MACHINE_D_PORT=9193
MACHINE_D_PASSWORD=changeme
